// Static storage: globals initialized in order of definition (dynamic ones calling functions), a
// function-local static initialized once on first pass (also in a recursion and per template
// instance), static members of a class template per instance, inline static members, statics
// whose initializer reads another static.
char trail[1024];
int pos = 0;
void note(const char* s) { while (*s) trail[pos++] = *s++; trail[pos++] = ' '; trail[pos] = 0; }

int counter = 0;
int next(const char* who) { note(who); return ++counter; }

int first = next("first");
int second = next("second") * 10 + first;

struct Reg
{
  int id;
  Reg(const char* who) : id(next(who)) {}
};
Reg r1{"r1"};
Reg r2{"r2"};

int localStatic(int depth)
{
  static int calls = next("local");
  if (depth > 0)
    return localStatic(depth - 1) + calls;
  return calls;
}

template<class T>
int perType()
{
  static int value = next(sizeof(T) == 4 ? "int" : "dbl");
  return value;
}

template<class T>
struct Counter
{
  static int made;
  static inline int seen = 100;
  Counter() { ++made; ++seen; }
};
template<class T>
int Counter<T>::made = 0;

struct Config
{
  static inline int base = 7;
  static const int derived;
};
const int Config::derived = Config::base * 3;

int main()
{
  printf("%s\n", trail);
  printf("%d %d %d %d\n", first, second, r1.id, r2.id);
  pos = 0;
  trail[0] = 0;
  int a = localStatic(3);
  int b = localStatic(0);
  printf("%d %d %s\n", a, b, trail);
  pos = 0;
  trail[0] = 0;
  int i1 = perType<int>(), d1 = perType<double>(), i2 = perType<int>();
  printf("%d %d %d %s\n", i1, d1, i2, trail);
  Counter<int> c1, c2;
  Counter<char> c3;
  printf("%d %d %d %d\n", Counter<int>::made, Counter<char>::made, Counter<int>::seen, Counter<char>::seen);
  printf("%d %d\n", Config::base, Config::derived);
  return 0;
}
